<title>SOUTH KOREA: Bank of Korea seen propping up won in afternoon.</title>
<headline>Bank of Korea seen propping up won in afternoon.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The central Bank of Korea was seen selling dollars again during late Friday afternoon trading to support the local currency, dealers said.</p>
<p>The central bank stepped in when the won/dollar rate fell to around the 844.40 level, they said.  </p>
<p>The won flucuated after the intervention, recovering to 844.20, then touching a low of 844.70, before regaining its feet again at 844.30.</p>
<p>&quot;There is so much import settlements that have to be met that it will be hard to keep the dollar down,&quot; said a local bank dealer.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5644</p>
